<title>BERMUDA: Bermuda exchange adds Mexican, Mekong Delta funds.</title>
<headline>Bermuda exchange adds Mexican, Mekong Delta funds.</headline>
<dateline>HAMILTON, Bermuda 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bermuda Stock Exchange said on Wednesday it had listed two new funds, one for investing in the Mekong Delta and a second for private equity placements in Mexico.</p>
<p>The Knight SC Mekong Fund was incorporated in the Cayman Islands and will invest in unlisted companies in Cambodia, the Yunnan province of China, Laos, Myanmar, Thailand and Vietnam, the exchange said in a news release.</p>
<p>The fund will be managed by King SC Mekong Management Ltd.</p>
<p>Also incorporated in the Cayman Islands is the Mexico Private Equity Fund, which will make private equity investments in Mexican manufacturing and processing groups focused on exports. It will be managed by Maguey Management Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Michael Connor - Miami newsroom, 305-374-5013</p>
